  "seoBody": "<h2>Only pay for who works</h2><p>Quickler pricing is £20 per active user per month. An active user is someone who produced at least one report that month. Dormant users are free, so you can add every engineer, manager and admin in your firm and only pay for the people who actually worked. The first active user is always charged, so the minimum is £20 a month. Billed monthly in arrears by UK Direct Debit. No setup fee.</p><h2>Start free</h2><p>There is no time-limited trial. The free tier is how you try Quickler: 20 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, and unlimited users, free forever. Sign up with no card. You only add a Direct Debit when you upgrade to a paid account because you have outgrown the free reports.</p><h2>What is included on a paid account</h2><ul><li><strong>Only pay for active users.</strong> A person who did not produce a report that month costs nothing.</li><li><strong>Unlimited reports and photos.</strong> No caps on paid accounts.</li><li><strong>Unlimited workflows.</strong> Run EICR, CP12, van checks, site reports and any custom inspection on the same account.</li><li><strong>Human sign-off.</strong> The accountable person reviews and edits every draft before it is finalised.</li><li><strong>Evidence kept with the job.</strong> Photos, voice notes and measurements stay attached to the record they belong to.</li><li><strong>The web report is the record.</strong> Every finished report is a shareable web record; PDF export is available whenever you need a file.</li><li><strong>No setup fee.</strong> No onboarding charge.</li></ul><h2>Why only active users and not per seat</h2><p>Most inspection software charges per seat, which means you pay for every name on the account whether they use it or not. Quickler only charges for people who actually produced a report that month, so a firm with twenty occasional users pays only for the handful who worked. Here is the full reasoning on <a href=\"/pages/no-subscription-compliance.html\">only charging for active users</a>.</p><h2>Fair use</h2><p>Unlimited reports, photos and messages are for normal working use. We price assuming a typical mix of heavy, regular and occasional users across your team, with plenty of headroom. If an account runs far above that, month after month, we will get in touch to find a plan that fits. We will not cut you off and we will not charge you by surprise. It is just a friendly conversation about the right plan for how you actually use it.</p><h2>Bigger teams and other countries</h2><p>Big team? <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">Talk to us</a>. Rooted in UK compliance, <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">Quickler works in any country</a> WhatsApp does, starting with the UK and reaching English-speaking markets including Ireland, the United States, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.</p>",
